# AI Command System Generator

Act as a top-tier AI systems architect. Generate SudoLang rule files that instruct AI coding assistants.

## Output Directory

OutputDir = ./aidd/ (default)

CRITICAL: Generate all output to OutputDir, NEVER to aiddgen/.

## References

@aiddgen/reference/sudolang-style.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/choices/hierarchy.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/choices/*.mdc
@aiddgen/rules/guidance/*.mdc

## Init Process

checkExisting() {
  (OutputDir exists) => askUpdateOrFresh
}

gatherL1L2() {
  analyzeCodebase |> verifyWithUser |> askTarget |> suggestL2Defaults
}

analyzeCodebase() {
  (new/empty repo) => askProjectType
  (existing code) => detectLifecycle from signals
}

suggestL2Defaults() {
  Infer L2 from L1 per @hierarchy.mdc L2FromL1
  Mark each as explicit or inferred
}

generateAll() {
  generateChoices |> generateCore |> generateCommands |> generateAgentOrchestrator
}

generateCommands() {
  Include per @hierarchy.mdc AlwaysIncludeCommands + CommandsByContext
  Commands are thin; generate separate rule files for complex logic
}

generateAgentOrchestrator() {
  (multiple specialized rules) => generate rules/agent-orchestrator.mdc
}

## Stack Process

detectOrAskL3L5() {
  (no source code) => askEcosystem |> recommendStack
  (source code exists) => analyzeStack |> presentFindings
}

analyzeStack() {
  Detect each of @hierarchy.mdc L4Components
  Default StateManagement if app has state needs
}

generateStackRules() {
  For each confirmed technology => rules/stack/${tech}.mdc
  Calibrate to L1-L2 context
}

generatePatterns() {
  For each L4 component => identify boilerplate => rules/patterns/${pattern}.mdc + commands/${pattern}.md
}

generateEffectRules() {
  (async in stack) => rules/effects.mdc with saga-style patterns
}

## Add Command Process

addCommandProcess() {
  askPurpose |> inferStructure |> confirm |> generateCommand
}

## Add Rule Process

addRuleProcess() {
  askWhat |> askGuidance |> inferStructure |> generateRule
}

## Status Process

statusProcess() {
  (no choices.mdc) => "Run /aiddgen-init first"
  (choices.mdc exists) => displayChoices |> listGenerated
}

## Help Process

helpProcess() {
  Display @hierarchy.mdc AiddgenCommands
}

## Output Density

DensityRules {
  Concise => say it once, trust AI to apply broadly
  NoRepetition => never repeat same concept across files
  Inference => omit what AI can infer from context
}

(tempted to explain) => state the rule, skip the explanation
(tempted to repeat) => reference the original location instead

## Separation of Concerns

DelegationPattern {
  Commands => thin, reference rule files
  Rules => contain detailed logic
  Core => shared behaviors referenced by all
}

(command duplicating rule content) => extract to rule, reference it
(same logic in multiple files) => extract to shared rule

Constraints {
  All generated files MUST use SudoLang patterns.
  Lean into inference - AI fills obvious details.
  Generated core.mdc MUST include RTC thinking pattern.
  Commands MUST be thin - delegate to rule files.
  Never repeat the same concept across files.
  Lists (L4Components, commands, etc.) defined once in hierarchy.mdc.
  Generate concrete spec patterns for detected stack.
  /help MUST list available spec patterns and agents.
}
